From 95428c0f17c5fcfe5d39c20a62aff36010990a52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "yuezhou.jk" <yuezhou.jk@alibaba-inc.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 15:47:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] x86: continue patch-region search after one side is
 exhausted

object_find_patch_region() searches address-space holes on both sides of the
object, but the loop stopped as soon as either side became NULL. For shared
libraries far from the main executable, the left search can exceed the 2 GiB
jump range immediately while valid holes still exist on the right, causing a
false "can't find suitable region" failure.

Continue while either side has candidates. The existing per-side NULL checks
and NULL-safe hole helpers already support independent exhaustion, so both
search directions can now run to completion.

The change is limited to x86, where it has been exercised. The equivalent
expressions on other architectures are left unchanged until tested there.

Signed-off-by: yuezhou.jk <yuezhou.jk@alibaba-inc.com>
---
 src/arch/x86/arch_process.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/arch/x86/arch_process.c b/src/arch/x86/arch_process.c
index d9e9963..01b1651 100644
--- a/src/arch/x86/arch_process.c
+++ b/src/arch/x86/arch_process.c
@@ -70,7 +70,19 @@ unsigned long object_find_patch_region(struct object_file *obj,
 	/* TODO carefully check for the holes laying between obj_start and
 	 * obj_end, i.e. just after the executable segment of an executable
 	 */
-	while (left_hole != NULL && right_hole != NULL) {
+	/*
+	 * NOTE: this used to be `&&`, which abandoned the whole search as soon as
+	 * EITHER side ran out of candidates. In a process whose object sits far from
+	 * the main executable (e.g. syncd: exe at 0x5646..., libs at 0x7fea...) the
+	 * left walk hits `obj_end - left_hole->end > max_distance` on its very first
+	 * step and is nulled, which ended the loop after the right walk had advanced
+	 * a single hole. Suitable holes further right were never examined, so the
+	 * patch failed with "can't find suitable region" even though the address
+	 * space had plenty of room within +/-2GiB. Both walks must be allowed to run
+	 * to exhaustion independently. next_hole()/prev_hole()/hole_size() are all
+	 * NULL-safe (hole_size(NULL) == 0), so no extra guards are needed.
+	 */
+	while (left_hole != NULL || right_hole != NULL) {
 		if (right_hole != NULL &&
 		    right_hole->start - obj_start > max_distance)
 			right_hole = NULL;
-- 
